		<h1>Privacy Policy & California Consumer Privacy Rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h1>
		<p><strong>Effective Date: July 27, 2026</strong> | <strong>Last Updated: July 27, 2026</strong></p>

		<div class="legal-alert">
			<strong>Important Notice for California Residents:</strong> GridPermit complies strictly with the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA). You have explicit rights regarding the collection, disclosure, and referral of your personal information to third-party licensed installers.
		</div>

		<h2>1. Overview & Information We Collect</h2>
		<p>GridPermit ("Company", "we", "us") operates an independent clean energy educational and analysis platform. When you utilize our savings calculators or request contractor matching services, we collect:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Identifiers:</strong> Name, physical address, ZIP code, email address, and phone number.</li>
			<li><strong>Property & Utility Information:</strong> Estimated monthly utility bills, current utility provider (e.g., PG&E, SCE, SDG&E), roof shaded status, and homeownership status.</li>
			<li><strong>Technical Data:</strong> IP address, browser type, device identifiers, and interactions with our web forms.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>2. How We Use & Share Your Information (Lead Referrals)</h2>
		<p>We use your information to calculate estimated solar and battery payback timelines and, upon your explicit request, to connect you with up to three (3) pre-vetted, licensed third-party solar contractors or engineering partners ("Installers").</p>
		<p>Under CCPA definitions, transferring your contact details to an installer in exchange for a lead referral fee may constitute a "sale" or "sharing" of personal information. By submitting a quote request, you authorize this referral under statutory compliance guidelines.</p>

		<h2>3. Telephone Consumer Protection Act (TCPA) Consent Notice</h2>
		<p>By submitting your phone number on GridPermit, you provide express written consent under the TCPA for GridPermit and its network of certified solar partners to contact you via telephone, automated dialing systems, artificial or prerecorded voice messages, and text/SMS messages regarding solar and battery estimates. Consent is not a condition of purchasing any property, goods, or services.</p>

		<h2>4. Your California Privacy Rights (Do Not Sell My Info)</h2>
		<p>As a California resident, you possess the right to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> Request disclosure of what personal data we have collected about you.</li>
			<li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> Request complete deletion of your personal data from our active databases.</li>
			<li><strong>Right to Opt-Out:</strong> Direct us not to sell or share your personal information to third parties.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>To exercise these rights, email our legal compliance team at <code>legal@gridpermit.com</code> with the subject line "CCPA Privacy Request".</p>

		<p style="margin-top: 3rem;"><a href="/">&larr; Return to GridPermit Homepage</a></p>
